    [BugFix]Avoid models that do not require LSE from using the KvQuantSFA operator. (#18540)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    Support KV quant sparse flash attention when return_lse is False.
    Previously, only the `return_lse=True` branch was handled using
    `torch.ops._C_ascend.npu_kv_quant_sparse_flash_attention_vllm`. This PR
    adds an `else` branch using
    `torch_npu.npu_kv_quant_sparse_flash_attention` to properly support
    attention execution when `return_lse` is set to False.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    No, this is an internal function enhancement/bugfix to support both LSE
    and non-LSE execution paths.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    - Run vllm bench
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/c4df37dfcc7f72ca41cd43801a468526ecf99a2b
    
    ---------
    
    Signed-off-by: caiqigang <cabbage_alex@hotmail.com>

